  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The hype train gives way too many notifications, especially when it's about to expire. In VR, they're very in your face and really immersion breaking, and just feel like an ad I was forced to see when I'm already a vrc+ member.\n\nWhy? Picture this: You're at furality. You're vibing to a really good dj set. You're immersed, dancing with your friends next to you, you feel really present in the space! and then you get a popup. A new friend about to come dance? ...no, someone just donated vrchat plus. Doesn't really impact me! I already have it! back to dancing! and then several more notifs of other folks dropping subs, makes sense, just try and ignore it. Then it dies down, no one else dropping gifts. Your immersion is Pretty Gone at this point, but you're still dancing.\n\nYou get back into it, feeling pretty immersed and in the space again. Then bam, another notif pops up. friend time? ...nope, just begging for someone else to gift vrc plus. Ok, ignore it, back to dancing. 30 seconds later, again, begging to donate. ignore it again. Start to get immersed once again, then glory be, one final notification that it's over. Back to dancing!!! ...only for someone to drop another gift sub, which resets everything.\n\nIt made me actively avoid some instances because I was just getting a drip feed of notifications that would ruin my experience. I don't want my phone to buzz at me at a concert, so I turn it on silent. VRC notifications are so much more immersion breaking and in your face, why can't I turn them off?",
